## 🏛️ SYSTEM IDENTITY

  Project  : Ram Rajya Society System — Python Backend
  Repo     : ramrajya-backend-python
  Language : Python 3.10+
  Framework: FastAPI
  ORM      : SQLAlchemy (async)
  Schemas  : Pydantic v2
  Auth     : JWT (HS256), OAuth2 scopes
  Testing  : Pytest + httpx (TestClient / AsyncClient)
  Docs     : Auto Swagger at /docs  (redoc at /redoc)


## 🗂️ PROJECT STRUCTURE (Intended)

  ramrajya-backend-python/
  ├── app/
  │   ├── main.py              ← FastAPI app instance, router include, startup
  │   ├── api/
  │   │   └── v1/              ← All versioned route files
  │   ├── core/
  │   │   ├── config.py        ← pydantic-settings: reads .env
  │   │   ├── security.py      ← JWT encode/decode, password hashing
  │   │   └── logging.py       ← Structured logging setup
  │   ├── models/              ← SQLAlchemy ORM models (tables)
  │   ├── schemas/             ← Pydantic v2 request / response schemas
  │   ├── crud/                ← Thin DB layer: create, read, update, delete
  │   └── tests/               ← Pytest: conftest.py + test_*.py files
  ├── .claude/
  │   ├── agents/              ← AI agent definitions for Claude Code
  │   └── skills/              ← Reusable AI skill instructions
  ├── ai-agents-main/          ← Source of agents+skills (reference copy)
  ├── .env                     ← Local secrets (never commit)
  ├── requirements.txt
  ├── progress.toon            ← Task tracker
  └── learn.toon               ← This file — knowledge base


## 🤖 AGENTS & SKILLS (Claude Code)

  ── Agents ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
  fastapi-backend   Senior Backend Dev
                    Builds endpoints, schemas, ORM models.
                    Enforces security checklist before writing code.
                    Reads: fastapi-standards, fastapi-porm, project-context

  fastapi-tester    QA Automation Engineer
                    Writes Pytest suites. Covers 401/403/422 security cases.
                    Reads: fastapi-testing, fastapi-standards, project-context

  ── Skills ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
  project-context   Shared env, DB config, architecture blueprint
  fastapi-standards PEP 8, API versioning, error codes, security rules
  fastapi-porm      Pydantic v2 model patterns, SQLAlchemy ORM helpers
  fastapi-testing   Pytest fixtures, AsyncClient, auth mocking patterns

  ── Agent Setup ─────────────────────────────────────────────
  Running /fastapi-backend <task>  inside Claude Code activates the agent.
  Skills are auto-read by agents from .claude/skills/<name>/SKILL.md


## 🔐 AUTHENTICATION & SECURITY

  Algorithm    : HS256 (JWT)
  Token Expiry : 30 minutes (access token)
  Scopes       : admin | user | read-only
  Protected endpoints return:
    401  — no token / expired token
    403  — valid token but insufficient scope
    422  — malformed request body (Pydantic validation)

  RULES (from fastapi-standards):
  - Never return ORM models directly — always use response_model
  - No raw SQL — use ORM queries
  - No hardcoded secrets — use .env via pydantic-settings
  - No synchronous I/O inside async routes


## 🗄️ DATABASE

  DB Type  : PostgreSQL (primary) or MySQL
  ORM      : SQLAlchemy (async sessions)
  Migrations: Alembic (track schema changes)

  Connection flow:
    .env → core/config.py (Settings) → database.py (engine + session) → crud/

  Placeholders to fill in .claude/skills/project-context/SKILL.md:
    {{API_BASE_URL}}   real API URL
    {{DB_HOST}}        database host
    {{DB_NAME}}        database name
    {{DB_USER}}        database user
    {{CORS_ORIGINS}}   allowed frontend origins


## 📡 API DESIGN RULES

  - All routes versioned under /api/v1/
  - HTTP verbs:  GET(read) POST(create) PUT(replace) PATCH(partial) DELETE
  - Standard status codes:
      200 OK · 201 Created · 204 No Content
      400 Bad Request · 401 Unauthorized · 403 Forbidden
      404 Not Found · 422 Unprocessable Entity · 500 Internal Server Error
  - Swagger must have summary, description, and example for every endpoint
  - response_model set on every route handler


## 📦 MODULES PLANNED

  Module        Route prefix           Key operations
  ─────────     ──────────────────     ──────────────────────────────
  Auth          /api/v1/auth           login, logout, refresh-token
  Users         /api/v1/users          CRUD, role assign
  Societies     /api/v1/societies      society registration & management
  Members       /api/v1/members        member onboarding, profiles
  Payments      /api/v1/payments       fee collection, receipts
  Notices       /api/v1/notices        announcements, circulars
  Maintenance   /api/v1/maintenance    maintenance requests, status
  Reports       /api/v1/reports        financial & activity reports


## 🧪 TESTING KNOWLEDGE

  Framework : pytest
  Client    : httpx.TestClient (sync) or httpx.AsyncClient (async)
  conftest  : defines fixtures — db session, test client, auth tokens

  Every module needs:
    test_<module>_create    — 201 happy path
    test_<module>_read      — 200 happy path
    test_<module>_update    — 200/204 happy path
    test_<module>_delete    — 204 happy path
    test_<module>_401       — missing/invalid token
    test_<module>_403       — wrong scope
    test_<module>_422       — bad input data

  Run tests:
    pytest app/tests/ -v
    pytest --cov=app --cov-report=term-missing


## 🔧 USEFUL COMMANDS

  # Start dev server
  uvicorn app.main:app --reload --host 0.0.0.0 --port 8000

  # Run migrations
  alembic upgrade head

  # Generate new migration
  alembic revision --autogenerate -m "describe change"

  # Run tests
  pytest app/tests/ -v

  # Check coverage
  pytest --cov=app --cov-report=html


